#!/usr/bin/env python3
# aeris:summary=Desktop pet (dragon or raven) on a transparent overlay
# aeris:group=desktop
# aeris:args=[run|start|quit|toggle|status|set dragon|raven|where desktop|bar]
"""aeris-pet: a small dragon companion for the desktop, outside any terminal.

It swims through the air like Haku: its body undulates as it moves, and its
fins flutter. On the ground it walks on four jointed legs (elbows and hocks
bent back, clawed paws) and tucks them back in flight. It rests, dances, flies on arcs,
perches on window title bars, pecks at crumbs, sleeps when idle, and says
things from the greetings file. It also watches battery, pending updates and
tailscale, and patrols when something needs attention.

  left click     dance and greet
  double click   fly to the top border of a window
  middle click   drop crumbs on the floor
  drag + throw   carry it, then let it fly
  right click    open the pet menu in the top bar (which pet, hide)

The pet menu lives in the AERIS bar (paw icon). Pets: dragon (default) or raven; the
choice is kept in ~/.local/state/aeris-pet/pet and picked up by the running pet.

  aeris-pet                 run the pet (one instance; a second start does nothing)
  aeris-pet set dragon|raven  choose the pet, starting it if it is not running
  aeris-pet quit            hide the pet
  aeris-pet where bar|desktop  live in the top bar (drawn by Quickshell, Bar/PetLane.qml)
                            or on the desktop overlay (this program)
  aeris-pet status          bar module JSON: {"text", "class", "pet", "running", "where"}

In bar mode this program does not run: the shell draws a small pet in the bar and
start/quit/toggle show or hide it there (hidden = ~/.local/state/aeris-pet/bar-hidden).

The pet's windows never take keyboard focus (no_focus rule, no popup grabs), so it
cannot swallow the keyboard.

The dragon is drawn on a full-screen transparent window, so Hyprland never has
to move it while it flies. Animation runs on the monitor's frame clock, so it
uses the screen's full refresh rate.

Test hooks: AERIS_PET_DEMO=1 drops crumbs shortly after start;
AERIS_PET_STATS=1 prints frame timing every five seconds.
"""
import fcntl
import glob
import signal
import sys
import json
import math
import os
import random
import struct
import subprocess
import threading
import time
import wave

import cairo
import gi

